  culture: `<p>Egyptians debate passionately about football, politics, prices and whose mother cooks best, and a loud argument can be friendly. Disagreement is softened with humour and terms of endearment: <i>ya 7abiibi, inta mish faahim 7aaga!</i> can be affectionate. Religion and national politics are sensitive with strangers; follow your host's lead.</p>`,
