  reading: { title: "Maktoub", text: [
    ["المصريين بيقولوا \"كله مكتوب\"، يعني كل حاجة مقدرة من ربنا.", "il-masriyyiin biy2uulu \"kullu maktuub\", ya3ni kull 7aaga m2addara min rabbina.", "Egyptians say “it's all written”, meaning everything is destined by God."],
    ["لما حد يفوته القطر، صاحبه يقوله: \"مش مكتوبلك تسافر النهارده\".", "lamma 7add yfuutu l-2atr, sa7bu y2ullu: \"mish maktuublak tsaafir innaharda\".", "When someone misses the train, a friend tells him, “It wasn't written for you to travel today.”"],
    ["الكلمة دي بتريح الناس وبتخليهم مايزعلوش أوي من الحاجات اللي مش في إيدهم.", "il-kilma di bitrayya7 in-naas w bitkhalliihum mayiz3aluush awi min il-7agaat illi mish fi iidhum.", "The word comforts people and stops them getting too upset over things out of their hands."],
    ["بس برضه في مثل بيقول \"اسعى يا عبد وأنا أسعى معاك\"، يعني لازم تحاول الأول.", "bass bardu fi masal biy2uul \"is3a ya 3abd w ana as3a ma3aak\", ya3ni laazim ti7aawil il-awwil.", "But there's also a proverb: “Strive, servant, and I'll strive with you”, meaning you have to try first."],
  ], questions: [
    { q: "What does kullu maktuub mean?", opts: ["Everything is destined", "Everything is written down", "Everything is finished", "Everything is clear"], a: 0 },
    { q: "What does the proverb at the end add?", opts: ["You still have to make an effort", "Never try too hard", "Trains are always late", "Friends bring luck"], a: 0 },
  ] },
