  culture: `<p>Ramadan in Egypt is festive: streets hung with lanterns (<i>fawaniis</i>), <i>mawaa2id ir-ra7maan</i> (free public iftar tables), TV series premieres and late-night outings. Non-Muslims aren't expected to fast, but eating in public during the day is discreet. Christians and Muslims exchange greetings on each other's feasts.</p>`,
